{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-jackson-q-bessel-contiguity","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:jackson-q-bessel-contiguity","kind":"proof","leanRef":"qou:QOU.QBeta.qbessel_first_kind_coeff_closed_form","text":"jackson-q-bessel-contiguity.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:jackson-q-bessel-contiguity\"></a><p>The first- and second-kind Jackson <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-Bessel functions have power-series coefficients <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_k</code> satisfying purely algebraic first-order contiguity recurrences in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nu</code>. The closed forms are proved. Computations verify the ratios symbolically and numerically. This formal-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> structural identity fixes the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">SU_q(1,1)</code> radial coefficient algebra.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jackson-q-bessel-contiguity.md","heading":"Proof","page":"b/prf-jackson-q-bessel-contiguity","qa":{"counts":{"pass":58,"fail":2,"warn":2,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":58},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Nuclear.QBeta.qbessel_first_kind_coeff_closed_form","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/MathlibExt/QBesselContiguityRecurrence.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
